<p>I don't know if that's a core part of canon - I've seen quite a few SCPs with an object-class of Thaumiel but without being explicitly level-5 only, and <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-3667">3667</a> has a separate &quot;level 3 clearance required&quot; section while still being Thaumiel-class.</p>
<p>In any case, the only people who would have the 3/4000 clearance necessary to see the low-clearance document would be researchers in Area-R01 and a few RAISA officials dealing with the documents. The former are isolated on Mars and could probably be safely given temporary clearance to know about this specific Thaumiel SCP; they could then be amnesticized before returning to Earth. The latter need to know the information in order to analyze the produced documents, and RAISA probably has its own internal system for dealing with classified information.</p>

